                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6838: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-12-09T09:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                                1925—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 9—2:24
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>521. My 517, December 7, 10 a.m. Following from American consul, Mukden: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 8, 1 p.m. Chang and his son are determined to make hard fight.
                            Young Chang has a strong position on the Liao. There is still a small
                            possibility that the Marshal can hold on. The city quiet.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
